  <div class="deck" id="deck">

    <section class="slide active" data-slide="1">
      <div>
        <div class="kicker">arxiv: 2604.08377</div>
        <h1>SkillClaw: Collective Skill Evolution for Multi-User LLM Agent Ecosystems</h1>
        <p class="subtitle">From static, manually installed skills to a closed-loop system where multi-user trajectories drive shared, evidence-grounded skill updates.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="content hero">
        <div class="panel">
          <h2>Let Skills Evolve Collectively with Agentic Evolver</h2>
          <ul class="bullets" style="margin-top:.6rem">
            <li>Aggregates trajectories from heterogeneous users and tasks.</li>
            <li>Diagnoses root causes through attribution over behavior traces.</li>
            <li>Mutates shared skills conservatively via verified acceptance.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <img src="/app/benchmark/assets/figure_1.jpg" alt="SkillClaw architecture overview figure" />
      </div>
      <div class="footer"><span>ML researchers & AI systems engineers</span><span>1 / 8</span></div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-slide="2">
      <div>
        <div class="kicker">Problem Framing</div>
        <h2>Agent Skills Remain Static After Deployment — Users Rediscover Solutions Independently</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="content two-col">
        <div class="panel">
          <h3 style="margin:0 0 .45rem;font-family:Sora;font-size:clamp(.9rem,1.3vw,1.15rem)">Static Skill Paradigm</h3>
          <ul class="bullets">
            <li>Skills are manually authored and installed once.</li>
            <li>Runtime failures do not systematically update skills.</li>
            <li>Users independently rediscover similar fixes.</li>
            <li>No ecosystem-level mechanism accumulates experience.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="panel">
          <h3 style="margin:0 0 .45rem;font-family:Sora;font-size:clamp(.9rem,1.3vw,1.15rem)">Desired Evolving Paradigm</h3>
          <ul class="bullets">
            <li>Interaction trajectories become reusable evidence.</li>
            <li>Skill mutations are proposed from diagnosed causes.</li>
            <li>Validated improvements synchronize to all users.</li>
            <li>System quality compounds through collective use.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="footer"><span>Core bottleneck: no closed-loop adaptation</span><span>2 / 8</span></div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-slide="3">
      <div>
        <div class="kicker">Architecture Overview</div>
        <h2>Closed-Loop Pipeline: From Multi-User Interaction to Shared Skill Evolution</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="content panel">
        <div class="diagram-grid">
          <div class="stage"><div class="num">Stage 1</div><h3>Evidence</h3><p>Collect trajectories from multi-user sessions exercising shared skills under diverse contexts.</p></div>
          <div class="stage"><div class="num">Stage 2</div><h3>Attribution</h3><p>Analyze success/failure traces to identify likely root causes in skill behavior.</p></div>
          <div class="stage"><div class="num">Stage 3</div><h3>Evolution</h3><p>Generate candidate skill mutations via agentic open-ended reasoning.</p></div>
          <div class="stage"><div class="num">Stage 4</div><h3>Distribution</h3><p>Validate and synchronize accepted updates back into the shared skill pool.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="arrowline">Multi-User Interaction → Session Collection → Agentic Evolver → Skill Synchronization → (Loop)</div>
        <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:.8rem;margin-top:.75rem;align-items:center;">
          <div style="font-size:clamp(.8rem,1.1vw,.96rem);color:var(--muted)">The loop converts isolated runtime experiences into collective, continuously improving capability.</div>
          <img src="/app/benchmark/assets/figure_1.jpg" alt="SkillClaw architecture figure" style="width:100%;max-height:min(34vh,260px);object-fit:cover;border-radius:.7rem;border:1px solid rgba(122,162,255,.35)"/>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="footer"><span>Four-stage closed loop</span><span>3 / 8</span></div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-slide="4">
      <div>
        <div class="kicker">Agentic Evolver</div>
        <h2>Evidence → Attribution → Evolution in Three Stages</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="content two-col">
        <div class="panel">
          <ul class="bullets">
            <li><b>Evidence Analysis:</b> ingest trajectory sets with outcomes, action traces, and context.</li>
            <li><b>Attribution:</b> diagnose whether failure stems from missing guidance, brittle logic, or scope gaps.</li>
            <li><b>Evolution:</b> draft candidate skill mutations and expected behavioral effects.</li>
            <li>Workflow is <b>reasoning-driven</b>, not fixed rule templates.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="panel">
          <h3 style="margin:0 0 .45rem;font-family:Sora;font-size:clamp(.9rem,1.3vw,1.12rem)">Why this matters</h3>
          <ul class="bullets">
            <li>Supports context-aware updates grounded in observed behavior.</li>
            <li>Handles open-ended failure modes across heterogeneous tasks.</li>
            <li>Enables conservative acceptance through downstream validation.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="footer"><span>Agentic reasoning over trajectory evidence</span><span>4 / 8</span></div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-slide="5">
      <div>
        <div class="kicker">Cross-User Signal</div>
        <h2>Cross-User Trajectory Aggregation Exposes Skill Behavioral Boundaries</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="content panel">
        <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:.9rem;min-height:0;">
          <div>
            <ul class="bullets">
              <li>Compatible systems include OpenClaw, CoPaw, IronClaw, PicoClaw, ZeroClaw, NanoClaw, NemoClaw.</li>
              <li>Diverse users invoke the same skill under distinct prompts, tools, and constraints.</li>
              <li>Aggregation reveals complementary success and failure signatures.</li>
              <li>Single-user traces are often insufficient to separate robust improvements from one-off patches.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="stage" style="height:100%">
              <h3 style="margin-top:0">Group Session Aggregation (Architecture Segment)</h3>
              <p style="font-size:clamp(.78rem,1.04vw,.94rem)">User A/B/C sessions feed a shared trajectory buffer. The evolver operates over grouped evidence to estimate where a skill generalizes vs. where it breaks, then proposes mutations with higher transfer potential.</p>
              <p style="margin-top:.45rem;font-size:clamp(.78rem,1.04vw,.94rem)"><b>Key effect:</b> richer boundary detection for when and why the current skill fails.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="footer"><span>Collective signal beats isolated trajectories</span><span>5 / 8</span></div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-slide="6">
      <div>
        <div class="kicker">Case Study A</div>
        <h2>Multimodal Creative Pipeline Skill — 6 Days of Evolution Attempts</h2>
        <p class="subtitle">Conservative verification retained only 1 of 6 candidate updates.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="content panel">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr><th>Date</th><th>Outcome</th><th>Rationale</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>2026-04-01</td><td class="badge-no">Rejected</td><td>Overfit to narrow prompt style; reduced robustness across variants.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>2026-04-02</td><td class="badge-no">Rejected</td><td>Introduced unnecessary branching; higher failure rate in edge tool states.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>2026-04-03</td><td class="badge-ok">Accepted</td><td>Improved step ordering and fallback guidance; net reliability gain.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>2026-04-04</td><td class="badge-no">Rejected</td><td>Regressed output consistency for multimodal handoff stage.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>2026-04-05</td><td class="badge-no">Rejected</td><td>Added verbosity without measurable execution benefit.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>2026-04-06</td><td class="badge-no">Rejected</td><td>Conflicted with existing validated constraints in skill pool.</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <div class="footer"><span>Accepted 1 / 6 attempts</span><span>6 / 8</span></div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-slide="7">
      <div>
        <div class="kicker">Case Study B</div>
        <h2>Git Push Auth-Fallback Skill — Iterative Refinement Over 6 Days</h2>
        <p class="subtitle">Three accepted updates before performance plateaued.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="content panel">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr><th>Date</th><th>Outcome</th><th>Rationale</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>2026-04-01</td><td class="badge-ok">Accepted</td><td>Added explicit auth fallback path for common remote mismatch.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>2026-04-02</td><td class="badge-no">Rejected</td><td>Candidate duplicated checks already encoded in base skill.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>2026-04-03</td><td class="badge-ok">Accepted</td><td>Improved token/SSH decision logic under ambiguous credential states.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>2026-04-04</td><td class="badge-no">Rejected</td><td>Triggered unnecessary retries, increasing latency without success gain.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>2026-04-05</td><td class="badge-ok">Accepted</td><td>Refined final fallback sequencing; higher completion on hard cases.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>2026-04-06</td><td class="badge-no">Rejected</td><td>No incremental gain beyond prior accepted version (plateau).</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <div class="footer"><span>Accepted 3 / 6 attempts</span><span>7 / 8</span></div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-slide="8">
      <div>
        <div class="kicker">Takeaways</div>
        <h2>Three Properties That Distinguish SkillClaw from Existing Systems</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="content two-col">
        <div class="panel">
          <ul class="bullets">
            <li><b>Collective evolution:</b> individual interactions improve a shared ecosystem.</li>
            <li><b>Fully automatic:</b> no manual curation required for routine updates.</li>
            <li><b>Agentic evolution paradigm:</b> open-ended reasoning drives skill mutation.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="panel">
          <h3 style="margin:0 0 .45rem;font-family:Sora;font-size:clamp(.9rem,1.3vw,1.12rem)">Implications</h3>
          <ul class="bullets">
            <li>Continuously improving agent systems become practical at scale.</li>
            <li>Validation-gated updates balance innovation with reliability.</li>
            <li>Multi-user ecosystems convert usage into compounding capability.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="footer"><span>Research-forward outlook for adaptive agent platforms</span><span>8 / 8</span></div>
    </section>

  </div>

  <script>
    (function () {
      const slides = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('.slide'));
      let index = 0;
      function show(i) {
        slides[index].classList.remove('active');
        index = (i + slides.length) % slides.length;
        slides[index].classList.add('active');
      }
      window.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {
        if (e.key === 'ArrowRight' || e.key === 'PageDown' || e.key === ' ') show(index + 1);
        if (e.key === 'ArrowLeft' || e.key === 'PageUp') show(index - 1);
      });
    })();
  </script>
</body>
</html>
